    ## Capability Gaps
  - (see Research Findings, updated below)
  + - **Multi-line edits on CRLF files fail (new, measured live, product-facing).** Codex 0.162.0 (#51203, 2026-10-08) shipped "preserve existing CRLF line endings in apply_patch by default". I probed mine in /tmp/crlf with b57d5831:
  +   - A single-line `edit_file` on a CRLF file **works** and keeps the `\r\n`.
  +   - A **two-line** old_text (`alpha\nbeta`, LF-joined as the model writes it) against `alpha\r\nbeta\r\ngamma\r\n` **fails**: `old_text not found in g.txt.` The file is untouched.
  +   - The failure message steers the model wrong. `📍 Nearest match at line 1` shows text identical to old_text, because `str::lines()` strips `\r`. The recovery hint says "Use read_file to see current contents, then retry with the exact text", which can't work, since the model can't see `\r`. The model then made up a wrong diagnosis ("trailing newline or the line gamma").
  +   - Mechanism: yoagent 0.25.2 `tools/edit.rs:105` does `content.matches(old_text)` with no line-ending handling. yoyo's `src/smart_edit.rs` wrapper has `try_whitespace_autofix` (l.463), but it only fires for `is_whitespace_only` matches, and its `extract_matched_text` / `.lines()` path drops the `\r` difference.
  +   - Fix seam: in SmartEditTool (yoyo-owned), when the file contains `\r\n` and old_text has bare `\n`, retry with both old_text and new_text translated to CRLF. Otherwise new_text would also introduce mixed endings. Add a note on success. Say "line endings" in the not-found error when that's the only difference.
  +   - The audience is Windows users (yoyo ships install.ps1) and any repo with CRLF files. Per CLAUDE.md's yoagent rule, also consider a yoagent issue, since EditFileTool is upstream.
  +   - Not probed: multi-line edits whose old_text already carries `\r\n`, mixed-ending files, and write_file on a CRLF file.
  + - Retry-After: Codex 0.162 now honours it. yoagent 0.25.2 `agent_loop.rs:2088` already does ("Server-provided Retry-After wins over backoff"), so this is **not** a gap.
