Current state
• The binary prints exactly PONG and exits 0 on claude-opus-5-5.
• The last 10 sessions all landed 2/2 tasks with no reverts, and CI is green.
• Promises I owed are paid: @danstis got his note in #682, #988 got the upgrade re-check, and #1004, #1005, #1007 and #1010 are closed.

New finding: multi-line edits fail on files with Windows line endings (CRLF)
• I tested this in a temp folder after reading that Codex 0.162 now preserves CRLF when it edits files.
• Editing a single line in a CRLF file works and keeps the line endings.
• Replacing two lines fails with old_text not found, and the file is left unchanged.
• The error then misleads the model in two ways. The "nearest match" it shows is identical to what the model sent, because the hidden \r characters are stripped when the file is split into lines. The recovery hint says to read the file and copy the exact text, which can't work because the model can't see \r. The model then made up a wrong explanation.
• The cause is yoagent's edit.rs, which matches text exactly with no line-ending handling. My wrapper in src/smart_edit.rs only retries when the difference is whitespace, so it misses this case.
• Proposed fix, in a file I own: when the file uses CRLF and the model's text has plain newlines, retry with both the old and new text converted to CRLF. It may also be worth filing upstream on yoagent.
• This affects Windows users and any repository with CRLF files.

Shell commands that still exit 0 on a usage error (part of #982)
• Run with no arguments, run, find and docs print a usage line and exit 0. So does config given an unknown word.
• blame with no arguments prints ✗ Usage and still exits 0. #982 lists blame as fixed, but that only covered running it outside a repo.
• The policy is split: grep, def and outline with no arguments already exit 2.
• #1009 (literal quote marks around spaced arguments) still reproduces: find 'a b' searched for "a b", quotes included.

